  "label": "Disliking a social media post is mapped onto the historical figure of Adolf Hitler",
  "description": "The text 'I don't like this post' is juxtaposed with the image of Adolf Hitler, who is historically associated with genocide and mass murder. The meme creates an analogical mapping where the trivial act of disliking a social media post is equated with the genocidal actions of Hitler, implying that such a response is justified or appropriate. This mapping is explicit through the visual-textual pairing, where Hitler's image serves as a symbolic representation of the extreme, violent response the text suggests.",
